Close the arm64 implementation class outside the base64 block

simdutf 7.7.1 closes the arm64 implementation class inside
SIMDUTF_FEATURE_BASE64, so builds without base64, such as the one VTE
uses, fail to compile on aarch64. The other targets already close it
after the block.

--- a/subprojects/simdutf/src/simdutf/arm64/implementation.h
+++ b/subprojects/simdutf/src/simdutf/arm64/implementation.h
@@ -284,8 +284,8 @@
                    char character) const noexcept;
   const char16_t *find(const char16_t *start, const char16_t *end,
                        char16_t character) const noexcept;
-};
 #endif // SIMDUTF_FEATURE_BASE64
+};
 
 } // namespace arm64
 } // namespace simdutf
